    "It was in a hall under the eastern quarter that the silt had sealed. He took her down by a stair that nobody else used."
    "It was a workshop. It was ten times the size of the one at Kettle House, and it was just as untidy. He had one of those tools in his pocket; he had carried it round the world."
    "In the middle of the floor was an air-heart, half built. Its maker had laid down the work one evening three thousand years ago, with every part set out in order beside it, and had never come back."
    "And the walls were alight."

    scene cg c18_archive_palm
    with dissolve
    "He laid his palm on the nearest. Pictures moved under it. They showed a pair of hands, long-fingered and broad, doing a thing with the pale metal that he had tried and failed to imagine at a bench in the Pale."
    "They did it slowly. They did it again when he asked."

